  "id": "descriptive-norm",
  "term": "descriptive norm",
  "definition": "A descriptive norm is the pattern of behavior that appears to be common in a group, which people may use as a guide for their own choices. In this context, it refers to conforming to what most people in an ingroup, outgroup, or overall set of people seem to do.",
